00:07:00.679 --> 00:07:07.539
The case on both sides of Gray County's nuisance wildlife pay is a provincial rule on one hand and a road call business on the other.

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:17.539
County Council passed updated bylaws in August. Five trappers, Byron Schwartz, Brian Aitkin, Tom Eastman, Dave McAllys, and Bob Cranenberg

00:07:17.539 --> 00:07:23.099
put their objections in a September 18 letter that sat on the November 12th committee of the whole agenda.

00:07:23.099 --> 00:07:29.039
Pay doubles on January 1st, 2027 from $25 to $50 a beaver.

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:34.079
Coyote and wolf payments go to $100, then climb with the consumer price index.

00:07:34.679 --> 00:07:37.479
Staff said those rates had sat still for more than 20 years.

00:07:38.019 --> 00:07:42.159
At a November 9th information session, county staff said the province no longer

00:07:42.159 --> 00:07:44.999
allows bounties for beavers, coyotes, or wolves.

00:07:45.319 --> 00:07:48.959
So a claim now needs county sign-off before any hunting or trapping starts.

00:07:48.959 --> 00:07:54.159
One staff member said the ministry was very clear that the county can no longer pay bounties

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:56.059
for coyotes or beavers or wolves.

00:07:56.719 --> 00:07:58.459
Landowner and trapper fill out a form.

00:07:58.899 --> 00:08:00.799
The county then opens a six-week window.

00:08:01.279 --> 00:08:04.939
Approval can take up to 10 days, staff said, and is usually faster.

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:08.439
Animals taken on public land no longer draw county pay.

00:08:09.019 --> 00:08:13.639
Work on a road allowance has to be authorized and paid by the road authority, and staff said

00:08:13.639 --> 00:08:17.499
those authorities stay responsible if a beaver hazard brings a tree down on the road.

00:08:17.499 --> 00:08:22.559
The Owen Sound Current has not confirmed with the ministry what the ministry actually told the county.

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:26.419
Trappers asked why Bruce County does not demand the same pre-approval.

00:08:26.859 --> 00:08:28.979
Staff said they could not speak for Bruce County.

00:08:29.519 --> 00:08:31.299
The five trappers welcomed the higher check.

00:08:31.899 --> 00:08:37.699
In the letter CKNX also reported they say the work is time-consuming and carries real operating costs

00:08:37.699 --> 00:08:41.799
and that going from a one-page form to five pages needs to be revisited.

00:08:42.219 --> 00:08:46.059
They argue municipal pay alone often does not make a road call worth doing.

00:08:46.059 --> 00:08:50.519
They reject the suggestion that taking money from both the town and the county is improper

00:08:50.519 --> 00:08:55.039
double dipping, and they warn the new limits could leave nuisance beavers on municipal roads

00:08:55.039 --> 00:08:56.979
and drains without a trapper willing to go.

00:08:57.539 --> 00:09:01.399
They want the county to reopen the rules with experienced local trappers at the table.

00:09:01.919 --> 00:09:05.099
The higher rates are scheduled for January 1st, 2027.

